# One calculation, many screens

If more than one component needs the same number (goals, units, leftover, revenue, %), put the math in a shared module and have every screen call it. Do not copy the formula into each Vue file.

## Campaign month progress (My results / Team results)

Source of truth: `getCampaignMonthView` in [`src/js/orderAuthority.js`](src/js/orderAuthority.js), which uses helpers in [`src/js/statsUtils.js`](src/js/statsUtils.js).

If My results or Team results look wrong again, change `getCampaignMonthView` (or the statsUtils helpers it calls). Do not patch `agentDashboard.vue`, `assignGoals.vue`, `agentCaseCard.vue`, `agentsPage.vue`, or reports separately.

Call it like:

```js
const view = getCampaignMonthView(order, dailyLogs, monthKey, agentId)
// view.myUnits / view.myGoal   — personal
// view.teamUnits / view.teamGoal — team
```

## When adding a new screen

- Import the existing helper. If it is missing a field, extend the helper and reuse it.
- Vue components format and render. They do not invent leftover, scaling, or month-cap logic.
- New shared math goes in `src/js/` (prefer `statsUtils.js` / `orderAuthority.js` for campaign stats).
